          "summary": "Extend product warranty to 12 months from delivery, remove the fixed December 31, 1999 sunset, make the malicious-code warranty continuous, and add a professional-and-workmanlike services warranty with a re-performance/refund remedy.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We need a warranty period that is meaningful in practice: 60 days measured from the Effective Date and capped at December 31, 1999 expires almost immediately and before most Customer deployments go live, so we have moved to twelve (12) months from delivery, kept the malicious-code warranty continuous, and added the standard professional and workmanlike warranty for the installation, implementation, support and professional services with a re-performance or refund remedy. If twelve months is not workable, we can accept ninety (90) days from delivery for the Software and thirty (30) days for services, with the same remedies.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0078",
              "oldText": "for a period of sixty (60) days from the Effective Date, but in no event not later than December 31, 1999 (the \"Warranty Period\")",
              "newText": "for a period of twelve (12) months from the date of delivery of the Software (the \"Warranty Period\")"
